From 3c1a3c5721bf2b3481f52c4e12f0ea0edf0cb282 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:43:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Security: unused request handlers removed, Security Review
 seal and wider watch, login redirect address

- 51 request addresses and 36 page hooks that no shipped page uses are removed from the web server (with the AiMesh
  allow-list rows that named them); a request for a removed address is logged once per address for one beta. The
  stock pages that only served them stop shipping, and their old addresses bounce to the Reaper page that does the job.
- Security Review: the accepted baseline is sealed (a fingerprint kept outside /jffs), so a baseline or rule change
  made outside the page shows every item as unreviewed; switching the review off only through the page's switch.
  The review watches more settings and Warden's list files, adopts newly watched items once on upgrade, and knows
  every form of Reaper's own scheduled jobs, matching each line exactly.
- Data export: the snapshot age is read with date -r, so a stale health snapshot is no longer pushed.
- Tweaks: the login page can redirect to an address the admin types (name and port), validated on save.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
